answer:
Because parameter markers cannot represent column names or SQL keywords like `ASC` and `DESC`, you must map user choices to a strict allow-list of fixed, application-owned values rather than appending the supplied text directly [SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet:007, SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet:006]. 

Map the user's selection using a switch statement or map to select the allowed column name or sort direction, and reject anything else [SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet:007]:

```java
String tableName;
switch(PARAM) {
  case "room":
    tableName = "roomTable";
    break;
  case "floor":
    tableName = "floorTable";
    break;
  default:
    throw new InputValidationException("unexpected table name");
}
```
